        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            DailyPlanner (“we,” “our,” or “us”) is a planning application
            designed to help users organize their daily tasks, schedules,
            and personal activities.
        </p>
        <p>
            We respect the privacy of our users and are committed to
            handling personal information responsibly. This Privacy Policy
            explains what information may be collected, how it is used,
            how it is protected, and what choices users have regarding
            their information.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
            Depending on the features used and how the application is
            configured, DailyPlanner may process the following information.
        </p>

        <h3>A. Account Information</h3>
        <p>
            When users register for an account, the application may collect
            a name, email address, and password or authentication credentials.
            Passwords should be securely handled by the authentication
            system and should not be stored in plain text.
        </p>

        <h3>B. Tasks and Planner Information</h3>
        <p>
            The application may store information entered by users, such as
            task titles, descriptions, schedules, reminders, and other
            planning details, to provide its main functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>Information processed by DailyPlanner may be used to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Create and manage user accounts.</li>
            <li>Authenticate users and provide access to the application.</li>
            <li>Save and organize tasks and schedules.</li>
            <li>Maintain application functionality and troubleshoot technical problems.</li>
            <li>Protect the application and its users against unauthorized access or misuse.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We use information only for purposes consistent with this
            Privacy Policy and the application's actual functionality.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Storage and Security</h2>
        <p>
            Information may be stored locally on the user's device or on
            a server or cloud service, depending on the application's
            actual configuration.
        </p>
        <p>
            We take reasonable measures to protect information against
            unauthorized access, loss, alteration, or disclosure. However,
            no method of electronic storage or transmission can be
            guaranteed to be completely secure.
        </p>
        <p>
            Users should keep their login credentials confidential and
            use a strong, unique password.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
        <p>
            We do not sell users' personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
            Personal information may be shared when necessary to provide
            an enabled application feature, operate a service used by the
            application, comply with applicable law, protect users, or
            fulfill another purpose disclosed to the user.
        </p>
        <p>
            If DailyPlanner uses third-party authentication, hosting,
            analytics, crash reporting, or other service providers, their
            relevant data practices should also be disclosed.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            DailyPlanner is not intended to collect personal information
            from children in violation of applicable privacy laws. Where
            required, appropriate consent and safeguards must be
            implemented before processing children's personal information.
        </p>
        <p>
            Parents or guardians who believe a child has provided personal
            information inappropriately may contact the developer.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
            Subject to applicable law, users may have the right to request
            access to, correction of, or deletion of their personal
            information and to raise concerns about how their information
            is processed.
        </p>
        <p>
            Users may contact the developer to make a privacy-related request.
        </p>

